# Quality Gate

1. `make build` — compiles binary.
2. `make test`  — runs `go test -v ./...`.
3. `make fmt`   - cleans whitespace and adds new lines to the end of files
4. `make lint`  — executes `ggo run github.com/golangci/golangci-lint/cmd/golangci-lint@latest run ./...`.

> A feature is **done** only when all four targets succeed with zero warnings and errors. **You have to run the quality gate**